                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Hard times.\nThis one is a Unity tower defense game, I think extremely indie since it's published and developed by a Russian guy, and well, it's quite clear since the first screens.\nBasically it has no menu, no backstory, nothing apart from a retro-style page that asks you to \"press start\" (which means click on the start text) and it puts you right into the game.\nAnd the game, well, it's the most basic tower defense you can imagine, and it has only 12 levels. There are as I said no tutorials, nothing. Ok, if you're quite experienced I think you don't need tutorials at all - you've got towers to build and upgrade, enemies coming from one side to the other one and such.\nThe game too has drawn too much from other games such as Kingdom Rush by adding for instance the option to call forth additional knights as a \"power\".\nThe music is overall quite absent, and the sound effects are very retro.. not that bad anyways, but it's a game that needs to be played with some sort of Youtube playlist.\nOverall, this looks very similar to other tower defense franchises in every aspect, apart from the of course less polished graphics and mechanics - the placement of the warriors, three per tower, the archer towers and so on.. everything is really recycled.\nMost of all, you've got just some info on your screen (money, go back, health points and waves remaining) and well.. the game is REALLY, REALLY slow and has NO fast forward functions.. there are games like Gemcraft which often have like 5x speed..\nSo be prepared, since it's very very very slow.. and not even that easy, trust me!\nThe maps themselves look quite the same of the Incursion, Cursed Treasure, Kingdom Rush etc. levels.. and I'd love to recommend this game, but really there are too many flaws in it.\nIt costs only 1€ and that's great, but it's all so ripped off from all the major tower defense games freely available all over the Internet.\nPlus, it has no trading cards even if the main page says so, as other players noted.\nSo, overall, it looks like that the developer tried to make a tower defense game by himself and some graphic elements are in fact new, but everything looks already played if you've ever been on Kongregate and similar sites, and there's an extreme lack of features: fast forward, tutorials, informations on upgrades and so on. You can't call waves early, there isn't even a pause button and the game goes on on tray too.. by the way if you play it, play it in full screen otherwise you won't read or distinguish anything, since the icons are too small\nAnd you've got only three tower types (warriors deployed on the road, archers and mages), and without tutorials you have to literally figure out by yourself what the upgrades will do - there's literally no text at all in the whole game.\nWhich is, as I said, 12-levels long, and you can't even choose them. They flow one after the other.\nSummarizing, I can't recommend it even if it has achievements and if it's an indie game costing only 1€. It has too many flaws, it's too slow and there are no functions at all, not even the speed up button; plus, you've got really limited choices in your towers and the relative upgrades, and there are no tutorials whatsoever.. so it's definitely not suitable for a gamer new to the genre. \nBeing a long-time tower defense player, it's also quite bad in my opinion the fact that everything is ripped off from other franchises, from the map designs to the types of towers; only the enemies look a bit different but that's it. And there's no upgrade system outside of the battle, it's very very very basic.\nPlay at your own risk and only if you are already into tower defense games, but for anyone else better avoid this title.",
